# VS Code Extension

Apply when editing `src/**/*.ts`. Read [doc/stack.md](../../doc/stack.md) for layout and commands. Subagent: `vscode-extension-agent`.

## Structure

Follow `layout` in `doc/stack.md`. Default:

- `src/extension.ts` — `activate` / `deactivate` entry
- `src/commands/` — command handlers
- `src/providers/` — Language Features, TreeDataProvider, etc.
- `src/webviews/` — Webview panels and messaging
- `src/utils/` — pure helpers

## Extension API rules

- Register all disposables via `context.subscriptions.push(...)`
- Command IDs must match `package.json` contributes exactly
- Keep `activate` lightweight — defer heavy work to first use
- Use `vscode.Uri.joinPath(context.extensionUri, ...)` for resource paths
- Secrets: `context.secrets` only — never `globalState` for tokens

## package.json sync

When adding commands, views, configuration, or activation events:

1. Update `doc/systemspec.md` first (spec-first)
2. Update `package.json` contributes
3. Implement in `extension.ts` or modules
4. Add integration test

## Naming

Full rules: [doc/coding-conventions.md](../../doc/coding-conventions.md).

| Target | Case | Example |
|--------|------|---------|
| Command ID | dot-separated | `acme.mdEditor.format` |
| Config key | camelCase section | `mdEditor.previewTheme` |
| Module files | kebab-case | `format-command.ts` |
| Provider classes | PascalCase | `OutlineTreeProvider` |

## Webview security

- Set CSP in HTML; use `webview.cspSource` for scripts/styles
- Restrict `localResourceRoots` to required directories
- Validate all `postMessage` payloads with type guards

## Before finishing

Use quality commands from `doc/stack.md` (`compile`, `test_single`, `typecheck`).
